# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the values you need.
# `.env` is git-ignored, so your key never reaches the repository.

# OPTIONAL. Leave this blank to use the free OpenStreetMap stack.
#
# With no key, doctor search uses Nominatim + Photon + Overpass (OpenStreetMap).
# Those return real facilities (names, addresses, phone numbers, coordinates)
# but no star ratings or individual consultant names.
#
# With a Google Places API (New) key, the app prefers Google instead and gains
# real doctor names, star ratings and review counts.
#
# How to get one:
#   1. Go to https://console.cloud.google.com/ and create (or pick) a project.
#   2. APIs & Services -> Library -> enable "Places API (New)".
#   3. APIs & Services -> Credentials -> Create credentials -> API key.
#   4. (Recommended) Restrict the key to the Places API and to your server IP.
#   5. Paste the key below. It looks like: AIzaSy...
GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY=
